TYPES.md §12.6, §1: a binding on an unknown case has the error type, so its uses report nothing more.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local variant V {
  a {
    n: Int
  }
  b
}

local fn f(v: V) -> Int {
  return match v {
    a(x) => x.n
    b => 0
    zz(y) => y.n
  }
}
-- findings.txt --
error[E3603]  a/a.canon:14:5
  zz(y) is not a case of a.V

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
